    {
      q: "Who maintains Indian Standard Time?",
      a: "IST is officially maintained by the CSIR-National Physical Laboratory (NPL) in New Delhi. NPL uses a network of cesium and hydrogen maser atomic clocks to generate and synchronize standard time, maintaining accuracy within nanoseconds."
    },
    {
