      a: "Yes. India briefly observed Daylight Saving Time during the Sino-Indian War of 1962 and the Indo-Pakistani Wars of 1965 and 1971 to reduce civilian energy consumption during wartime emergencies."
    },
    {
      q: "What is the IANA time zone identifier for India?",
      a: "The official IANA Time Zone Database identifier for India is `Asia/Kolkata` (formerly registered as `Asia/Calcutta`)."
    },
    {
      q: "What is the time difference between India and New York?",
      a: "During the winter (when New York is on EST, UTC-5), India (IST, UTC+5:30) is 10.5 hours ahead of New York. During the summer (when New York is on EDT, UTC-4), India is 9.5 hours ahead of New York."
    },
    {
      q: "What is the time difference between India and London?",
      a: "During the winter (when London is on GMT, UTC+0), India (IST, UTC+5:30) is 5.5 hours ahead of London. During the summer (when London is on BST, UTC+1), India is 4.5 hours ahead of London."
    },
    {
      q: "What is the time difference between India and Sydney?",
      a: "During the winter in Sydney (AEST, UTC+10), Sydney is 4.5 hours ahead of India. During the summer in Sydney (AEDT, UTC+11), Sydney is 5.5 hours ahead of India."
